WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.296 --> 00:00:02.728
- [Narrator] If you
know doughnuts, you know

00:00:02.728 --> 00:00:05.556
the pink doughnut box,
especially if you're familiar

00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:06.389
with Southern California,
which has hundreds of

00:00:06.389 --> 00:00:07.222
doughnut shops,

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:10.602
most with the pink boxes.

00:00:11.523 --> 00:00:13.201
But while you may recognize the box,

00:00:13.201 --> 00:00:15.161
you may not know it's central to a story

00:00:15.161 --> 00:00:17.911
about chasing the American dream.

00:00:22.202 --> 00:00:26.369
The pink box phenomenon all
started with a man named Ted.

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:28.851
Ted Ngoy came to California
as a Cambodian refugee

00:00:28.851 --> 00:00:29.934
in the 1970s.

00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:32.930
He got into the donut
business and became the owner

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.260
of dozens of shops.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.762
Ted sponsored other refugees
and taught them the business

00:00:37.762 --> 00:00:40.257
and helped them open their own shops.

00:00:40.257 --> 00:00:43.790
Since Ted used the pink
boxes, so did everybody else.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.483
Ted became known as the Doughnut King.

00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:47.316
- My name is Mayly Tao and
I am the Doughnut Princess

00:00:47.316 --> 00:00:48.149
of L.A.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.298
- [Narrator] The Doughnut
Princess's great uncle,

00:00:54.298 --> 00:00:57.725
the one and only Doughnut King, Ted Ngoy.

00:00:57.725 --> 00:01:00.193
He taught Mayly's parents
the business in the 1980s

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.241
and they started this shop.

00:01:02.241 --> 00:01:04.588
Mayly took it over a few years ago.

00:01:04.588 --> 00:01:07.550
And beyond Mayly, Ted's
legacy lives on through,

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.100
you guessed it, those pink boxes.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.612
- When we came to L.A., my
parents owned a doughnut shop

00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:14.280
for 26 years.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.324
We use the pink doughnut boxes.

00:01:16.324 --> 00:01:19.709
In the Asian community,
red is a lucky color,

00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:21.815
so therefore, using the pink box,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.584
it's no coincidence about it.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.088
- The pink box is
overwhelmingly the favorite

00:01:27.088 --> 00:01:29.403
of the doughnut shop industry.

00:01:29.403 --> 00:01:31.567
- [Narrator] That's Len
Bell, he should know.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:34.765
His company manufacturers
about 12 to 15 million

00:01:34.765 --> 00:01:36.851
doughnut boxes every year.

00:01:36.851 --> 00:01:37.684
- Cheers!

00:01:40.864 --> 00:01:42.503
- [Narrator] While the
pink boxes are still

00:01:42.503 --> 00:01:44.671
an iconic part of the doughnut landscape,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.542
owners are putting a new spin on things.

00:01:47.542 --> 00:01:49.098
Mayly makes some of the same doughnuts

00:01:49.098 --> 00:01:50.817
her parents used to make,
but like everything,

00:01:50.817 --> 00:01:53.149
times are a changin'.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:55.241
- When I took the business
over from my parents,

00:01:55.241 --> 00:01:57.123
they were using the generic pink boxes

00:01:57.123 --> 00:02:00.560
that you see everywhere, but
our doughnuts were not generic,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.254
and I needed to reflect that upon our new,

00:02:03.254 --> 00:02:04.893
upgraded boxes.

00:02:04.893 --> 00:02:06.944
- [Narrator] And what does your
mom think about that, Mayly?

00:02:06.944 --> 00:02:09.458
- [Mayly] My mom does not
really approve of the new boxes.

00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:10.723
They're a little bit more expensive,

00:02:10.723 --> 00:02:12.853
and it's not really what she's used to,

00:02:12.853 --> 00:02:16.370
but I think it's a sign
of new doughnut times.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.287
- [Narrator] Yum, sounds delicious.

